> The version already has that identifier followed by a counter, so the counter should go up, not restart from zero.

The fix: in `work/repo/classes/semver.js`, inside the `case 'pre'` block of `SemVer.prototype.inc`, the trailing `if (identifier)` block was changed. Previously it compared only `this.prerelease[0]` against the whole `identifier` string (`compareIdentifiers(this.prerelease[0], identifier) === 0`), so a dotted identifier like `rc.next` never matched the first prerelease part `rc`, and the prerelease was always replaced with `[identifier, base]` (counter reset to 0). Now the identifier is split on `.` into `ids`; it checks whether `ids` forms a prefix of `this.prerelease` (using `compareIdentifiers` per part), and only when a numeric counter exists right after that prefix does it keep the already-incremented prerelease; otherwise it falls back to `[identifier, base]` (or `[identifier]` when `identifierBase === false`).

The changed code (read it in the file for the exact current state) is roughly:

```js
if (identifier) {
  let prerelease = [identifier, base]
  if (identifierBase === false) {
    prerelease = [identifier]
  }
  const ids = identifier.split('.')
  const isPrefix =
    ids.length <= this.prerelease.length &&
    ids.every((id, i) => compareIdentifiers(this.prerelease[i], id) === 0)
  const counter = isPrefix ? this.prerelease[ids.length] : undefined
  if (!isPrefix || counter === undefined || isNaN(counter)) {
    this.prerelease = prerelease
  }
}
```

